Tunic of Riddosan Quest	25	{"kind":"quest","title":"Tunic of Ridossan Quest","wikiPath":"/Tunic_of_Ridossan_Quest","sources":[{"kind":"quest","where":"Paineel","detail":"Start zone"},{"kind":"quest","where":"Royal Guard Sheltuin","detail":"Quest giver"}],"components":[{"name":"Reagent pouch","qty":3,"wikiPath":"/Reagent_pouch"}],"rewards":[{"text":"Tunic of Ridossan","item":"Tunic of Ridossan","wikiPath":"/Tunic_of_Ridossan"}],"card":{"title":"Tunic of Ridossan Quest","lines":["Minimum Level: 1 (RECCOMEND 25+)","Classes: All","Related Zones: Clan Runnyeye, Najena, Qeynos Aqueducts, The Feerrott, The Warrens, West Freeport","Related NPCs: Driana Poxsbourne, Lyris Moonbane, goblin janitor"]},"links":["Paineel","Royal Guard Sheltuin","Clan Runnyeye","Najena","Qeynos Aqueducts","The Feerrott","The Warrens","Freeport","Driana Poxsbourne","Lyris Moonbane","Goblin janitor","Tunic of Ridossan","Cold Iron","Leggings of Ridossan","Heavy Locked Chest","Thick Glass Jar","Green river sludge","Vile Substance","Goblin Janitor","RunnyEye Citadel","Putrid substance","Reagent pouch","Bloodsabers","Opal Dark Briar","Corrupt Qeynos Guards","Guards of Qeynos","Priests of Life","Sealed Jar","Harbinger of Bertoxxulous","Empty Jar","Heretics","Deepwater Knights","Gate Callers","Craftkeepers","Crimson Hands"],"dialogue":[{"npc":"Royal Guard Sheltuin","text":"According to the evidence we've uncovered, it appears the kobolds are nothing but pawns to harass us. Or perhaps even all of Odus. If they wish to play these games, then we'll humor them. We'll take their pawn with one of our knights. Will you be the knight, ______?"},{"npc":"Royal Guard Sheltuin","text":"Then you will deliver this chest for us. Don't worry about what's inside it. Although we enjoy our solitude, we do make allies. We also make use of those allies. We will do so now. Take the chest to Lyris Moonbane below the human city of Qeynos. You will then follow her instructions and complete any tasks she assigns you. In return, she will send you back with what we wish. Fear is our armor."},{"npc":"Lyris Moonbane examines the lock on the chest and pulls a black key from a pouch at her hip. The lock clicks open. Her eyes widen as she carefully opens the chest, revealing a pile of platinum coins and a small note. After admiring the coins she takes the note and reads it. The necromancer glances up, then at her spectral pet who then hands you a glass jar. She","text":"Are you ready for your first [assignment], Erudite?"},{"npc":"Lyris Moonbane","text":"We have just the thing for your friends back home. It will take some doing, but the pay off will be lovely indeed. In that jar you must combine 4 substances. You'll need two portions of a [goblin..source], one portion of Green river sludge, and one [portion of an experimental nature] that an agent of ours is working on. Bring the mixture back to me and we'll speak again."},{"npc":"Lyris Moonbane","text":"The goblins of Antonica are known for their filthy habits and unclean practices. They often carry a menagerie of diseases and conditions. A more concentrated form of this aspect of goblin life cannot be found anywhere else but in the sewers of their citadel in the Serpent Spine. They must have workers who maintain the sewers. Find them and find the substance."},{"npc":"Lyris Moonbane","text":"The ogres of Oggok don't spend much time on sanitation, so naturally their kind harbors many diseases. This is easily apparent in the river that runs near their city, Greenblood. Down at the very bottom of the river is where the ancient plagues have come to rest and hibernate. Once the sludge is mixed in with the other substances, those glorious blessings of Bertoxxulous will most assuredly awaken."},{"npc":"Lyris Moonbane","text":"We have an agent studying in Freeport. Well, she actually isn't in Freeport proper but rather under it, in the sewers. Her name is Driana Poxsbourne. When you find her, tell her I have sent you for the substance. She will most likely have a task for you to complete before she can give you the fourth portion. Obey her."},{"npc":"Driana Poxsbourne","text":"Ahh, wonderful work, _______. Here is the substance...don't spill it! HAHAHAaahhahehehe...yes...you don't want to spill that, heheh."},{"npc":"Lyris Moonbane's eyes light up with childish glee as she takes the jar containing the disgusting and deadly substance. From her pouch she removes a gob of putty and a gem carved into the likeness of a flying insect. After sticking the putty to the lid of the jar, she mashes the carved gem into the putty and hands the jar back you. She then","text":"This is the Harbinger of Bertoxxulous. When the gem is brought near the kobold lair it will enchant the substance. You must then [deliver] the substance."},{"npc":"Lyris Moonbane","text":"You'll need to find the source of the kobold water supply and pour the substance into it. Once you do that, the disease will infest whatever living organisms it comes in contact with so do yourself a favor and leave the area quickly. You can then take the empty jar to your master for your reward."},{"npc":"Royal Guard Sheltuin","text":"Well done, _______! Now we need only wait for the kobolds to start dying off and our plan will be complete. Should only take 8 years or so. One such as yourself will wear this ancient armor well. The Tunic of the crusader Ridossan is now yours. He shall watch over and praise you in your triumphs... your defeats on the other hand... well, never mind that."},{"npc":"Driana Poxsbourne","text":"Hail! _______, You best not be associating yourself with the likes of Najena."}],"fetchedAt":"2026-09-23T05:28:32.410Z","outOfEra":false}
